  {
    "id": "m00-c-0004",
    "module": 0,
    "section": "Networking Essentials",
    "domain": "D0",
    "kind": "list",
    "front": "The six classic TCP flags",
    "back": "- **SYN**: open a connection\n- **ACK**: acknowledge data\n- **FIN**: close gracefully\n- **RST**: abort immediately\n- **PSH**: push data to the application now\n- **URG**: urgent pointer is valid\n\n(ECE and CWR carry congestion signals.)",
    "tags": [
      "tcp",
      "tcp-flags"
    ],
    "sources": [
      "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9293",
      "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc3168"
