    "section": "Networking Essentials",
    "domain": "D0",
    "kind": "term",
    "front": "ARP",
    "back": "Maps an **IPv4 address to a MAC address** on the local link. Replies are cached and never authenticated, so a host accepts replies it never asked for. This is the root of ARP spoofing.",
