    "module": 0,
    "section": "Operating System Essentials",
    "domain": "D0",
    "kind": "term",
    "front": "SUID bit",
    "back": "Octal **4000**, shown as `s` in the user execute slot (`-rwsr-xr-x`). The program runs with the **file owner's** privileges. Root-owned SUID binaries are a classic privilege-escalation path.\n\nFind them: `find / -perm -4000 -type f 2>/dev/null`",
    "tags": [
      "linux",
      "permissions",
      "suid"
    ],
    "sources": [
      "https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man7/inode.7.html",
      "https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man1/find.1.html"
    ],
    "verify": false,
    "rev": 1
  },
  {
    "id": "m00-c-0019",
    "module": 0,
    "section": "Operating System Essentials",
    "domain": "D0",
    "kind": "term",
    "front": "SGID and sticky bit",
    "back": "**SGID (2000)**: runs with the group's privileges; on a directory, new files inherit its group.\n\n**Sticky (1000, `t`)**: in a shared directory such as `/tmp`, only a file's owner can delete or rename it.",
    "tags": [
      "linux",
      "permissions"
    ],
    "sources": [
      "https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man7/inode.7.html",
      "https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/html_node/File-permissions.html"
    ],
    "verify": false,
    "rev": 1
  },
  {
